ds":[{"text":"1902","at":{"s":"mythFact","w":"1902"},"d":1.3}],"sfx":[{"lib":"motor_hum","at":{"s":"hook","w":"fan"},"d":1.4},{"lib":"drip","at":{"s":"problem","w":"drips"},"d":1.3},{"lib":"water_rush","at":{"s":"fix1","w":"drains"},"d":1.2},{"lib":"motor_hum","at":{"s":"fix2","w":"compressor"},"d":1.5}],"chimes":[{"s":"name"},{"s":"mythFact","w":"1902"},{"s":"congrats"}]},"codeShots":true,"why":"A portable air conditioner standing on the kitchen floor, cut open: a fan beside an icy coil above a tray, a compressor and a hot coil below, a duct to a vent in the wall. The camera stays on the unit; the opening is close on the fan and the frosting coil.","hold":true},"sentences":[{"role":"hook","text":"If you blow a fan through an icy coil, you have an air conditioner."},{"role":"problem","text":"But the cold coil pulls water from the air, and it drips onto the floor."},{"role":"fix1","text":"So you add a tray and a hose that drains the water away."},{"role":"problem2","text":"But now the coil warms up, and warm air blows into the room."},{"role":"fix2","text":"So you add a compressor that pumps coolant to keep the coil cold."},{"role":"name","text":"This is an air conditioner."},{"role":"how","text":"The heat goes to a hot coil and out through the wall."},{"role":"myth","text":"And comfort is not why air conditioning was invented."},{"role":"mythFact","text":"Willis Carrier designed it in 1902 so printing paper would not swell."},{"role":"finish","text":"Add louvers, a display and a filter."},{"role":"congrats","text":"Congratulations, you have built an air conditioner."}]}